Hello!
> I want to assign an R matrix to a java matrix. I supposed it was
> something easy like this
> "REXP x=re.eval("matrix(1:9,3,3)");
> double m[][]=x.asMatrix();"

A method that works for me is simply getting the matrix row-wise and
assigning the rows to the rows of a java matrix. Like:

for(int i=0; i<rows; i++) {
  matrix[i] = rengine.eval("rmatrix[" + i + ",]").asDoubleArray();
}

Might not be the most elegant, but works just fine ;)

Hope it helps,
-Wojtek Dabrowski
